{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Moses said.</b> Rashi's comment: this passage was said to him while he stood before Pharaoh. That is, it was said to Pharaoh from Moses' mouth, and proof of this: for if it were so, that it was said to Moses from the mouth of HaShem, why did Rashi not explain thus by 'and YHWH said to Moses'? Rather it is so, that Moses said it to Pharaoh on his own initiative, just as he declared the warning of the plague of locusts, as is stated in the Pesikta and in the Yelamdenu regarding this passage. <b>Like midnight.</b> — 'Who establishes the word of His servant' — this is HaShem, who fulfilled the word of Moses His servant who said 'like midnight.'" "<b>Like midnight.</b> When midnight arrives — as in 'you shall go out in the month of the spring' (i.e., at the arrival of the time). Here it is appropriate to write a kaf, 'when the time arrives,' but at the time of the actual event it is appropriate to say בחצי הלילה, with a bet." "<b>I am going out.</b> Since he does not heed the voice of My emissary — I shall go down Myself in My glory."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The comment on כחצת הלילה appears to allude to Isaiah 44:26 מקים דבר עבדו; פרש״‎י in the first sentence refers to Rashi's commentary."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:02.021991416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}